module main

-- §8 h-level — there is NO compiler-owned intrinsic h-level synthesis.
--
-- The doc assumes "compiler-owned intrinsic rules for the usual prelude types"
-- so that e.g. 'IsSet Bool', 'IsContr Unit', 'IsSubsingleton Void' synthesize.
-- THIS IMPLEMENTATION DOES NOT: the h-level traits (IsContr/IsSubsingleton/
-- IsProp/IsSet/IsGroupoid) are deliberately surfaced as bare nameable markers
-- (their proof-producing members cannot be synthesized for neutral terms), and
-- the only h-level instance in the prelude is 'instance IsSet String'.  So
-- 'IsSet Bool' is UNSOLVED — a sound under-derivation (a conservative analysis
-- may always answer "unknown"), not a soundness bug.
--
-- (Pinned with 'IsSet Bool' specifically because the doc lists it as a "pass";
-- it does not pass here.  IsContr/IsSubsingleton/IsProp goals over Unit/Void
-- behave identically — all unsolvable.)  The intrinsic-synthesis PASS cases are
-- DEFERRED to P2 pending the compiler-owned h-level rules.

let probe = summon (IsSet Bool)

--! mode check
--! assertDiagnostic error E_UNSOLVED_IMPLICIT
